More Vulnerabilities That Can Be Paid (721–730)
721. Improper Validation of Account Recovery Tokens
Account Recovery Token Prediction
Account recovery tokens are predictable or reusable, allowing attackers to take over accounts.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
722. Insecure Handling of API Error Messages
Verbose API Error Disclosure
APIs return detailed error messages revealing internal logic or database information.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
723. Improper Validation of Subscription APIs
Subscription Manipulation
Attackers modify subscription parameters to gain premium access for free.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $10,000
724. Insecure Handling of User Profile APIs
User Profile Authorization Bypass
Attackers access or modify other users’ profile information.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $7,000
725. Improper Validation of Download Counters
Download Counter Manipulation
Attackers manipulate download counters to bypass usage limits.
💰 Typical payout: $200 – $4,000
726. Insecure Handling of Payment Webhooks
Payment Webhook Forgery
Attackers forge webhook notifications to fake successful payments.
💰 Typical payout: $1,000 – $15,000
727. Improper Validation of Referral Systems
Referral Reward Abuse
Attackers manipulate referral systems to generate unlimited rewards.
💰 Typical payout: $400 – $8,000
728. Insecure Handling of Analytics APIs
Analytics Data Exposure
Analytics APIs expose internal usage data or user information.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
729. Improper Validation of File Download Tokens
Download Token Reuse
Download tokens can be reused or guessed to access private files.
💰 Typical payout: $300 – $6,000
730. Insecure Handling of System Maintenance Endpoints
Maintenance Endpoint Exposure
Maintenance endpoints reveal system controls or allow administrative actions.
💰 Typical payout: $500 – $9,000
